Requirements: 29   with obligations: 28   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] Plausible defects are enumerated for an obligation in one step, and the
    verdict on each of them is reached in a separate step that covers one obligation at
    a time.
    -> separate-enumeration-and-verdict-steps  [functional/explicit]
       Plausible defects are enumerated for an obligation in one step, and the verdict
       on each defect is reached in a separate step that covers one obligation at a
       time.

[constraint-01] The plausible defects for an obligation are enumerated by a call of
    their own.
    -> enumerate-defects-by-separate-call  [functional/explicit]
       The plausible defects for an obligation are enumerated by a call of their own.

[constraint-02] The verdict on an enumerated defect is reached by a call separate from
    the one that enumerated it.
    -> verdict-by-separate-call  [functional/explicit]
       The verdict on an enumerated defect is reached by a call separate from the one
       that enumerated it.

[constraint-03] A verdict call carries the defects of a bounded number of obligations.
    -> bounded-obligations-per-verdict-call  [boundary/explicit]
       A verdict call carries the defects of a bounded number of obligations.

[constraint-04] That number of obligations is configurable.
    -> configurable-obligation-bound  [functional/explicit]
       The number of obligations carried by a verdict call is configurable.

[constraint-05] That number of obligations is part of the recorded request.
    -> recorded-request-includes-obligation-bound  [invariant/explicit]
       The number of obligations carried by a verdict call is part of the recorded
       request.

[constraint-06] The enumeration request is determined by the obligation's text and by
    the changed code.
    -> enumeration-request-derived-from-text-and-changes  [functional/explicit]
       The enumeration request is determined by the obligation's text and by the changed
       code.

[constraint-07] The enumeration request is not determined by the tests mapped to the
    obligation.
    -> enumeration-request-independent-of-mapped-tests  [invariant/explicit]
       The enumeration request is not determined by the tests mapped to the obligation.

[constraint-08] Editing a test mapped to one obligation leaves a different obligation's
    enumerated defects unchanged.
    -> editing-mapped-test-preserves-other-obligation-defects  [regression/explicit]
       Editing a test mapped to one obligation leaves a different obligation's
       enumerated defects unchanged.

[constraint-09] Adding a test mapped to an obligation leaves that obligation's
    enumerated defects unchanged.
    -> adding-test-leaves-defects-unchanged  [regression/explicit]
       Adding a test mapped to an obligation leaves that obligation's enumerated defects
       unchanged.

[constraint-10] The review pipeline reaches its defect verdicts through the separated
    steps.
    -> review-pipeline-uses-separated-defect-steps  [functional/explicit]
       The review pipeline reaches its defect verdicts through the separated enumeration
       and verdict steps.

[constraint-11] The change does not reduce the defects the tool identifies.
    -> tool-identifies-no-fewer-defects  [invariant/explicit]
       The change preserves the number of defects the tool identifies.

[constraint-12] Two runs over the same obligations and the same changed code enumerate
    the same defects.
    -> same-inputs-same-defects  [regression/explicit]
       Two runs over the same obligations and the same changed code enumerate the same
       defects.

[constraint-13] Two runs over the same obligations and the same changed code reach the
    same verdicts.
    -> same-inputs-same-verdicts  [regression/explicit]
       Two runs over the same obligations and the same changed code reach the same
       verdicts.

[constraint-14] Tests issue no live model calls.
    -> tests-avoid-live-model-calls  [compatibility/explicit]
       Tests issue no live model calls.

[exclusion-01] How a rating is derived from the defect verdicts, which is #252.
    -> exclude-rating-derivation-from-defect-verdicts  [regression/explicit]
       The change does not alter how a rating is derived from the defect verdicts.

[exclusion-02] Which tests are mapped to an obligation.
    -> exclude-test-mapping-from-change  [regression/explicit]
       The change does not alter which tests are mapped to an obligation.

[exclusion-03] How an obligation is derived from a requirement.
    -> exclude-obligation-derivation  [functional/explicit]
       The change leaves the derivation of an obligation from a requirement out of
       scope.

[exclusion-04] Reporting a rating that could not be reproduced, which is #254.
    -> exclude-unreproducible-rating  [functional/explicit]
       The change leaves reporting a rating that could not be reproduced out of scope.

[exclusion-05] Choosing the number of obligations per call for cost or latency.
    -> exclude-call-count-optimization  [functional/explicit]
       The change leaves choosing the number of obligations per call for cost or latency
       out of scope.

[exclusion-06] Whether a defect verdict is correct about the test it describes.
    -> exclude-defect-verdict-correctness  [functional/explicit]
       The change leaves whether a defect verdict is correct about the test it describes
       out of scope.

